{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "ev-study-intro",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Washington EV charging: forecast and trace the evidence\n",
        "\n",
        "[![Aner](../assets/aner-logo.svg)](https://anerlang.org)\n",
        "\n",
        "This notebook runs the exact native source in [ev_charging.aner](ev_charging.aner). Open the repository root in the compatible Aner editor/notebook integration so `data/` and `generated/` resolve there. Create a fresh empty `generated/` directory before running; native exports deliberately reject existing files.\n",
        "\n",
        "The frozen case asks how county EV registrations might grow over twelve months, where projected growth coincides with limited public L2 inventory and renter context, and which priorities survive the declared scenario assumptions. The inputs are public observations, not invented demonstration data. The future projection remains conditional.\n",
        "\n",
        "The code checks the panel, reports source/transform provenance, evaluates 12 historical forecasting origins, generates 1,000 moving-block bootstrap paths per county, verifies exact one-worker/four-worker path values and seeds, and exports native numeric CSVs. The CSV column dictionary is [docs/output-columns.md](../docs/output-columns.md).\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "id": "ev-native-study",
      "metadata": {
        "aner": {
          "source_path": "code/ev_charging.aner",
          "source_sha256": "848a4fd37f8ff3e1e08a4b65a10a8a9f5733fced157884af7577cfafd5827151"
        }
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "// Run from the repository root with a fresh generated/ folder.\n",
        "// The bundled input tables are frozen public-data snapshots; no downloads occur.\n",
        "import aner.data\n",
        "import aner.parallel\n",
        "import aner.random\n",
        "import aner.math\n",
        "\n",
        "// Failed input contracts stop the native run before any output files are saved.\n",
        "fn require(condition: Bool, message: String) -> Unit {\n",
        "    if condition { return }\n",
        "    print(\"INPUT_ERROR: \" + message)\n",
        "    let rejected: Result<Bool, String> = Result.err(message)\n",
        "    let rejected_input = rejected.unwrap()\n",
        "}\n",
        "\n",
        "fn numeric_fips(code: String) -> Int64 {\n",
        "    var value = 0\n",
        "    var digit = 0\n",
        "    while digit < code.len() {\n",
        "        let parsed_digit = \"0123456789\".find(code.get(digit))\n",
        "        require(parsed_digit >= 0, \"FIPS must contain only decimal digits\")\n",
        "        value = 10 * value + parsed_digit\n",
        "        digit += 1\n",
        "    }\n",
        "    return value\n",
        "}\n",
        "\n",
        "// Native CSV export has numeric value_N columns; see docs/output-columns.md.\n",
        "fn export_row(parameters: List, iteration: Int64, seed: Int64) -> List {\n",
        "    return cast<List>(parameters.get(iteration))\n",
        "}\n",
        "\n",
        "fn validate_inputs(monthly: DataTable, counties: DataTable) -> Unit {\n",
        "    require(data.rows(counties) == 39, \"The frozen Washington case requires 39 counties\")\n",
        "    var accounted = 0\n",
        "    var county = 0\n",
        "    var first_calendar = -1\n",
        "    var final_calendar = -1\n",
        "    while county < data.rows(counties) {\n",
        "        let fips = data.text(counties, county, \"county_fips\")\n",
        "        require(fips.len() == 5 && fips.starts_with(\"53\"), \"Expected five-digit Washington FIPS\")\n",
        "        if county > 0 {\n",
        "            require(data.text(counties, county - 1, \"county_fips\").compare(fips) < 0,\n",
        "                \"County FIPS must be unique and sorted\")\n",
        "        }\n",
        "        require(!data.is_missing(counties, county, \"public_l2_ports\") &&\n",
        "            !data.is_missing(counties, county, \"public_dc_ports\") &&\n",
        "            !data.is_missing(counties, county, \"renter_share\"), \"Frozen county context must be present\")\n",
        "        require(data.integer(counties, county, \"public_l2_ports\") >= 0 &&\n",
        "            data.integer(counties, county, \"public_dc_ports\") >= 0, \"Port counts must be nonnegative\")\n",
        "        let renters = data.number(counties, county, \"renter_share\")\n",
        "        require(renters >= 0.0 && renters <= 1.0, \"Renter share must lie in [0, 1]\")\n",
        "        let history = data.collect(data.filter(monthly, data.col(\"county_fips\") == fips),\n",
        "            max_rows: 300, max_bytes: 1048576, batch_rows: 128)\n",
        "        require(data.rows(history) >= 48, \"At least 48 county months are required\")\n",
        "        let start_index = data.integer(history, 0, \"month_index\")\n",
        "        var previous_calendar = -1\n",
        "        var row = 0\n",
        "        while row < data.rows(history) {\n",
        "            let date = Date.try_parse(data.text(history, row, \"month\") + \"-01\").unwrap()\n",
        "            let calendar = 12 * date.year() + date.month()\n",
        "            if row == 0 {\n",
        "                if county == 0 { first_calendar = calendar }\n",
        "                require(calendar == first_calendar, \"All counties need the same first month\")\n",
        "            } else { require(calendar == previous_calendar + 1, \"Calendar months must be consecutive\") }\n",
        "            require(data.integer(history, row, \"month_index\") == start_index + row,\n",
        "                \"Month indices must be consecutive and unique\")\n",
        "            let stock = data.integer(history, row, \"ev_total\")\n",
        "            require(stock >= 0 && stock <= data.integer(history, row, \"all_vehicles\"),\n",
        "                \"EV stock must be bounded by all-vehicle registrations\")\n",
        "            previous_calendar = calendar\n",
        "            row += 1\n",
        "        }\n",
        "        if county == 0 { final_calendar = previous_calendar }\n",
        "        require(previous_calendar == final_calendar, \"All counties need the same forecast origin\")\n",
        "        accounted += data.rows(history)\n",
        "        county += 1\n",
        "    }\n",
        "    require(accounted == data.rows(monthly), \"Unmatched or duplicate county identities in monthly input\")\n",
        "}\n",
        "\n",
        "fn nonnegative(value: Float64) -> Float64 {\n",
        "    if value < 0.0 { return 0.0 }\n",
        "    return value\n",
        "}\n",
        "\n",
        "// Circular three-month blocks preserve short runs of net registration changes.\n",
        "// Assumes the last 24 monthly increments remain representative; no causal claim.\n",
        "fn bootstrap_stock(parameters: List, iteration: Int64, seed: Int64) -> List {\n",
        "    let initial = cast<Float64>(parameters.get(0))\n",
        "    let changes = cast<List>(parameters.get(1))\n",
        "    var change = 0.0\n",
        "    var block = 0\n",
        "    while block < 4 {\n",
        "        let start = random.integer(low: 0, high: changes.len() - 1, seed: seed, draw: block)\n",
        "        var offset = 0\n",
        "        while offset < 3 {\n",
        "            change += cast<Float64>(changes.get((start + offset) % changes.len()))\n",
        "            offset += 1\n",
        "        }\n",
        "        block += 1\n",
        "    }\n",
        "    return List(nonnegative(initial + change),\n",
        "        nonnegative(initial + 0.75 * change), nonnegative(initial + 1.25 * change))\n",
        "}\n",
        "\n",
        "fn drift(levels: List, origin: Int64) -> Float64 {\n",
        "    let level = cast<Float64>(levels.get(origin))\n",
        "    return nonnegative(level + 0.5 * (level - cast<Float64>(levels.get(origin - 24))))\n",
        "}\n",
        "\n",
        "var monthly_schema = data.schema()\n",
        "monthly_schema = data.column(monthly_schema, \"county_fips\", \"String\", false)\n",
        "monthly_schema = data.column(monthly_schema, \"county\", \"String\", false)\n",
        "monthly_schema = data.column(monthly_schema, \"month\", \"String\", false)\n",
        "monthly_schema = data.column(monthly_schema, \"month_index\", \"Int64\", false)\n",
        "monthly_schema = data.column(monthly_schema, \"ev_total\", \"Int64\", false)\n",
        "monthly_schema = data.column(monthly_schema, \"all_vehicles\", \"Int64\", false)\n",
        "let monthly = data.collect(data.scan_csv(\"data/ev_monthly.csv\", monthly_schema, \"NA\"),\n",
        "    max_rows: 20000, max_bytes: 4194304, batch_rows: 256)\n",
        "print(monthly.receipt())\n",
        "print(data.provenance(monthly))\n",
        "\n",
        "var context_schema = data.schema()\n",
        "context_schema = data.column(context_schema, \"county_fips\", \"String\", false)\n",
        "context_schema = data.column(context_schema, \"county\", \"String\", false)\n",
        "context_schema = data.column(context_schema, \"latitude\", \"Float64\", false)\n",
        "context_schema = data.column(context_schema, \"longitude\", \"Float64\", false)\n",
        "context_schema = data.column(context_schema, \"public_l2_ports\", \"Int64\", true)\n",
        "context_schema = data.column(context_schema, \"public_dc_ports\", \"Int64\", true)\n",
        "context_schema = data.column(context_schema, \"renter_share\", \"Float64\", true)\n",
        "let counties = data.collect(data.scan_csv(\"data/county_context.csv\", context_schema, \"NA\"),\n",
        "    max_rows: 39, max_bytes: 1048576, batch_rows: 64)\n",
        "print(data.provenance(counties))\n",
        "\n",
        "validate_inputs(monthly, counties)\n",
        "let county_rows = List()\n",
        "\n",
        "// Optional: parallel.cluster(config: \"private.cluster\") after explicit enrollment.\n",
        "// County and month identities never depend on worker or completion order.\n",
        "let execution = parallel.local(workers: 4)\n",
        "print(\"RESULT,county_fips,county,latest_month,observed_ev,forecast_ev,p10,p90,delta075,delta125,drift_mae,persistence_mae,projected_ev_per_l2,projected_ev_per_dc,renter_share\")\n",
        "var county_index = 0\n",
        "while county_index < data.rows(counties) {\n",
        "    let fips = data.text(counties, county_index, \"county_fips\")\n",
        "    let history = data.collect(data.filter(monthly, data.col(\"county_fips\") == fips),\n",
        "        max_rows: 300, max_bytes: 1048576, batch_rows: 128)\n",
        "    print(data.provenance(history))\n",
        "    let levels = List()\n",
        "    var row = 0\n",
        "    while row < data.rows(history) {\n",
        "        levels.append(Float64(data.integer(history, row, \"ev_total\")))\n",
        "        row += 1\n",
        "    }\n",
        "    let last = levels.len() - 1\n",
        "    let initial = cast<Float64>(levels.get(last))\n",
        "    let changes = List()\n",
        "    var month = last - 23\n",
        "    while month <= last {\n",
        "        changes.append(cast<Float64>(levels.get(month)) - cast<Float64>(levels.get(month - 1)))\n",
        "        month += 1\n",
        "    }\n",
        "    let paths = parallel.repeat(iterations: 1000, task: bootstrap_stock,\n",
        "        parameters: List(initial, changes), execution: execution, seed: 20261028 + county_index,\n",
        "        max_bytes: 1048576)\n",
        "    // Verify the same ordered numerical values and derived seeds on one worker.\n",
        "    let replay = parallel.repeat(iterations: 1000, task: bootstrap_stock,\n",
        "        parameters: List(initial, changes), execution: parallel.local(workers: 1),\n",
        "        seed: 20261028 + county_index, max_bytes: 1048576)\n",
        "    var sample = 0\n",
        "    while sample < paths.rows() {\n",
        "        require(paths.seed(iteration: sample) == replay.seed(iteration: sample), \"Replay seed mismatch\")\n",
        "        var output = 0\n",
        "        while output < paths.cols() {\n",
        "            require(paths.value(iteration: sample, column: output) ==\n",
        "                replay.value(iteration: sample, column: output), \"Replay numerical value mismatch\")\n",
        "            output += 1\n",
        "        }\n",
        "        sample += 1\n",
        "    }\n",
        "    print(\"REPLAY,\" + fips + \",1000,3,seeds_and_values_identical\")\n",
        "    paths.save_csv(\"generated/bootstrap-\" + fips + \".csv\")\n",
        "    print(paths.summary())\n",
        "    let ordered = paths.column(column: 0)\n",
        "    ordered.sort()\n",
        "    var drift_error = 0.0\n",
        "    var naive_error = 0.0\n",
        "    var origin = last - 23\n",
        "    while origin <= last - 12 {\n",
        "        let actual = cast<Float64>(levels.get(origin + 12))\n",
        "        drift_error += math.abs(actual - drift(levels, origin))\n",
        "        naive_error += math.abs(actual - cast<Float64>(levels.get(origin)))\n",
        "        origin += 1\n",
        "    }\n",
        "    let forecast = drift(levels, last)\n",
        "    var l2_pressure = \"NA\"\n",
        "    var dc_pressure = \"NA\"\n",
        "    var renters = \"NA\"\n",
        "    if !data.is_missing(counties, county_index, \"public_l2_ports\") {\n",
        "        let l2 = data.integer(counties, county_index, \"public_l2_ports\")\n",
        "        if l2 > 0 { l2_pressure = String(forecast / Float64(l2)) }\n",
        "    }\n",
        "    if !data.is_missing(counties, county_index, \"public_dc_ports\") {\n",
        "        let dc = data.integer(counties, county_index, \"public_dc_ports\")\n",
        "        if dc > 0 { dc_pressure = String(forecast / Float64(dc)) }\n",
        "    }\n",
        "    if !data.is_missing(counties, county_index, \"renter_share\") {\n",
        "        renters = String(data.number(counties, county_index, \"renter_share\"))\n",
        "    }\n",
        "    print(\"RESULT,\" + fips + \",\" + data.text(counties, county_index, \"county\") + \",\" +\n",
        "        data.text(history, last, \"month\") + \",\" + String(initial) + \",\" + String(forecast) + \",\" +\n",
        "        String(cast<Float64>(ordered.get(99))) + \",\" + String(cast<Float64>(ordered.get(899))) + \",\" +\n",
        "        String(nonnegative(initial + 0.75 * (forecast - initial))) + \",\" +\n",
        "        String(nonnegative(initial + 1.25 * (forecast - initial))) + \",\" +\n",
        "        String(drift_error / 12.0) + \",\" + String(naive_error / 12.0) + \",\" +\n",
        "        l2_pressure + \",\" + dc_pressure + \",\" + renters)\n",
        "    county_rows.append(List(numeric_fips(fips), initial, forecast,\n",
        "        cast<Float64>(ordered.get(99)), cast<Float64>(ordered.get(899)),\n",
        "        nonnegative(initial + 0.75 * (forecast - initial)),\n",
        "        nonnegative(initial + 1.25 * (forecast - initial)), drift_error / 12.0,\n",
        "        naive_error / 12.0, data.integer(counties, county_index, \"public_l2_ports\"),\n",
        "        data.integer(counties, county_index, \"public_dc_ports\"),\n",
        "        data.number(counties, county_index, \"renter_share\")))\n",
        "    county_index += 1\n",
        "}\n",
        "let forecast_rows = parallel.repeat(iterations: county_rows.len(), task: export_row,\n",
        "    parameters: county_rows, execution: parallel.local(workers: 1), seed: 20261028,\n",
        "    max_bytes: 1048576)\n",
        "forecast_rows.save_csv(\"generated/county-forecasts.csv\")\n",
        "print(forecast_rows.summary())\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "ev-study-next",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Continue the complete case\n",
        "\n",
        "After this notebook succeeds, run the two companion native programs from the same repository root:\n",
        "\n",
        "```sh\n",
        "aner run code/county_priorities.aner --max-steps 50000000\n",
        "aner run code/maps.aner --max-steps 50000000\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "[County priorities](county_priorities.aner) reads the newly generated native forecasts, computes all nine scenario combinations and their percentile-weighted ranks in Aner, reports zero-L2 counties separately, and exports the per-county rank ranges. [Maps](maps.aner) reads the bundled 2025 shoreline-clipped county GeoJSON and frozen station CSV, without an optional map pack, and exports static SVG and HTML. The [website viewer](https://anerlang.org/applications/ev-charging/stations.html) adds local pan, zoom, and county/station selection; its [builder](https://github.com/abastias/AnerWeb/blob/codex/ev-application-publication/scripts/build-ev-map-viewer.mjs) and [browser controls](https://github.com/abastias/AnerWeb/blob/codex/ev-application-publication/scripts/ev-map-viewer.js) live in the website repository. The [map-update manifest](../evidence/map-update-manifest.json) and [native county map](../evidence/stations-counties.svg) retain the updated rendering evidence. The original TIGERweb station assignments, forecasts, and ranks remain unchanged. These computations run entirely in Aner.\n",
        "\n",
        "The study's six stable candidates are Douglas, Cowlitz, Snohomish, Kitsap, Grant and Thurston. The nine parameter settings produce three distinct top-ten rankings, driven by renter weight; they are not nine independent validations or a probability of being correct. The p10/p90 bootstrap range is uncalibrated. Current port inventories, renter context, and registration stocks retain different observation periods.\n",
        "\n",
        "Read the [methods](../docs/methods.md), [source notes](../docs/data-sources.md), and [research](../docs/research.md) before interpreting a construction or funding decision. For Aner documentation and installation, visit [anerlang.org](https://anerlang.org).\n"
      ]
    }
  ],
